<title>JAPAN: Japan June lead imports down 48.6 pct yr/yr-MOF.</title>
<headline>Japan June lead imports down 48.6 pct yr/yr-MOF.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's refined lead imports in June fell by 48.6 percent to 893 tonnes from 1,739 tonnes in the same month a year earlier, Finance Ministry data issued on Tuesday showed.</p>
<p>The following is a breakdown (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		   June 97	    May 97	 June 96</p>
<p> Total	     893		572		1,739</p>
<p>Major suppliers:</p>
<p>China		508		202		  861</p>
<p>Australia	  188		187		  440</p>
<p>Cumulative imports in the first six months of 1997 were 20,736 tonnes, against 22,292 tonnes in the same period a year earlier.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3-3432-7391</p>
</text>
